# Both deploy/ Dockerfiles use the repo root as their build context (COPY paths reach across the
# whole repo). Without this, `COPY runner-dashboard/ ./` in deploy/web/Dockerfile would overwrite
# the Linux-native node_modules `npm ci` just installed with whatever node_modules happens to exist
# on the host (Windows/macOS binaries the same npm ci call would never produce) - a real risk, not
# hypothetical, caught during D0's own review round on a machine that actually had node_modules
# checked out. This also keeps the build context Docker actually has to transfer to a sane size.
.git
.gradle
.idea
**/build
runner-dashboard/node_modules
runner-dashboard/dist
runner-dashboard/coverage
deploy/.env

# Runtime events/logs/artifacts a real run produces under the repo root when *not* running in a
# container (e.g. this repo's own default `runner.*-dir` values in application.yml) - irrelevant to
# either image and occasionally large.
build/runner-events
build/runner-logs
build/runner-artifacts
allure-results
test-results
*.log
